bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    linux_secure_server_perf_runtime_blockers_2026-08-14, 0, "Doc read in full; reproducers in doc/09_report/perf/linux_secure_server_compare_2026-08-14.md, no fix recorded"
    linux_secure_server_perf_runtime_blockers_2026-08-14, 1, "2026-11-26 Linux aarch64 (DGX GB10, tip 79445b063c4, seed fb80903917d6d5f5). The DB insert_present failure is a driver bug, not a PureDatabase bug. db_crud_compare_driver.spl:37 compared row.? (which returns T?, a pass-through per syntax_quick_reference) with want: bool, so the comparison was always unequal and the driver exited 2 at stage=insert. The <invalid-heap:...> text is only how the seed renders a class value: unwrap() and a plain class render the same way. Fix: row.is_some() != want (:37) and row.is_none() (:72). Seed run: rc 2 -> 0, and all five stages pass (insert 556us, where 103us, update 189us, delete 252us, txn 265us). HTTP: static_listener_publication_contract_spec 2/2 PASS on aarch64. Native: NOT verified. The Stage 2 from cd29cfa8b64c (stage2-admitted, 2026-11-22) cannot native-build the driver closure: MIR/codegen ICEs in common.encoding.external_text, common.search.ranking, dbfs_engine.fts.search, io.external_file and io.file_text_session block the link, both on tip and on its own pinned tree. So the original native invalid-array-handle and the HTTP listener are still unproven on aarch64. Separate checker gap, not filed: the seed accepts i64? != bool without a type error."

